# NOlida — Cline Rules

## Brand Name (locked)
- The product name is "NOlida" (capital N, capital O, lowercase
  "lida").
- Never use "noLIDA", "Nolida", or any other casing in user-facing
  text or internal references.
- The only exception is the npm package name in package.json, which
  stays lowercase for npm compatibility.
- Infrastructure identifiers are ALSO exempt and must never be renamed,
  because renaming them breaks something real and buys nothing:
  the git remote (`noLIDA-platform/noLIDA.git`), the `nolida_session`
  cookie, the `nolida/*` Cloudinary upload folders, and the `nolida/`
  application directory. Branding is text; these are addresses.


## Stack (never deviate)
- Next.js 16 (App Router)
- React 19 with React Compiler enabled
- TypeScript strict mode — never plain JavaScript
- Plain CSS with CSS variables — never Tailwind, never CSS-in-JS
- PostgreSQL via Supabase
- pg for database access
- bcryptjs for password hashing — NEVER argon2
- zod for validation

## Architecture rules
- Server Components by default
- "use client" only on leaf components that need interactivity
- Route Handlers are thin: parse -> validate -> call service -> return
- Business logic in src/lib/server/services/
- SQL only in src/lib/server/repositories/
- Third-party SDK imports only in src/lib/server/adapters/
- No component imports from src/lib/server/
- No secrets outside src/lib/server/ or .env.local
- Imports use `@/*` alias, never ../../ chains
- Auth/wallet/payment routes: export const runtime = "nodejs"

## Brand rules (locked)
- Primary: #6366F1
- Accent cyan: #22D3EE
- Accent magenta: #D946EF
- Error / Sign Out: #DC2626
- Brand color is FIXED. Users can only toggle light/dark theme.

## Money rules (never break)
- All balance mutations inside a Postgres transaction with row locks

## Preventing Broken Imports

- Before starting ANY new work, read `docs/CODEBASE-REFERENCE.md` first.
- Every import used in the codebase must be listed in that document. If an import is not listed, it does not exist — do not use it.
- This file is the single source of truth for import paths, package names, service functions, repository functions, and component prop types.
- Always copy the closest working page as a template for new pages and components.
- After any edit, run `npm run build` to catch import errors before committing.

